# tools/ability_descs.exempt -- abilities that do NOT need a description yet.
#
# This is the other half of tools/ability_descs.live. Every ability with a
# ClassAbilities name row (src/Tables.cpp) either needs a description (it is
# in ability_descs.live) or is recorded here as not needing one yet. An entry
# here means "no description required yet", not "never will". tools/
# check_ability_descs.sh's fourth assertion is the ratchet: any newly granted
# ability must land in one of these two files or the check fails, so this
# list SHRINKS over time as abilities move to ability_descs.live -- it never
# grows except when a genuinely new CA_ constant appears.
#
# Format: one CA_ name per line. A line whose first character is '#' is a
# comment. Anything after the name on its own line, separated by whitespace,
# is also a comment (see the CA_WEATHER_SENSE line below).
#
# Most of the 39 entries below are monster-only abilities granted through
# ABILITY() in lib/mon*.irh: a polymorphed player can hold one and will see
# its bare name, exactly as today (docs/specs/2026-09-20-ability-descriptions-
# spec.md, "The 39 that stay bare").
#
# Two more abilities were investigated and are NOT listed below, because
# neither one is a real, reachable ability at all:
#   - CA_BANKED_SHOT has no ClassAbilities name row and is not even a defined
#     CA_ constant in inc/. It exists only as text inside a comment,
#     lib/prestige.irh:2408 ("/* Ability[CA_BANKED_SHOT,+1] at 10th level; */").
#   - CA_DISARM_MAGIC_TRAP has no live ClassAbilities name row either: its
#     row is commented out at src/Tables.cpp:3566, its only grant line is
#     commented out at lib/classes.irh:2580, and its case in
#     src/Sheet.cpp:601 is commented out too.
# Both are granted nowhere and read nowhere. They are recorded here in prose,
# not as list entries, so nobody re-derives the same dead end; they are not
# real CA_ names for the check to validate against ClassAbilities.
CA_ACROBATIC_FIGHTING
CA_AIR_MASTERY
CA_AURA_OF_MENACE
CA_BLACK_MAGIC
CA_BLOOD_MAGIC
CA_BONUS_SCHOOL
CA_BOOK_OF_SHADOWS
CA_BOOST_RESISTS
CA_BOOST_SPELLS
CA_CHANNELING
CA_CONTACT_MIND
CA_CRAFT_PSICRYSTAL
CA_DEATH_AFFINITY
CA_EARTH_MASTERY
CA_EARTHMELD
CA_FAMILIAR
CA_GASEOUS_FORM
CA_INSPIRE_ALLIES
CA_INVOKE_THE_LAND
CA_KARMIC_IMMUNITY
CA_LIFE_AFFINITY
CA_OPPORTUNIST
CA_PLANT_MASTERY
CA_PSIONICS
CA_PURGE_MAGIC
CA_REGEN
CA_SENSE_MAGIC
CA_SIZE_ADVANTAGE
CA_SLIPPERY_MIND
CA_SPAWN
CA_STALKER
CA_TELEPATHY
CA_TEMPRATURE_TOL
CA_TUNNEL
CA_TURN_RESISTANCE
CA_WALLWALK
CA_WATER_MASTERY
CA_WEATHER_SENSE  # dead in a different way: granted nowhere, its only grant line is commented out at lib/domains.irh:947
CA_WHITE_MAGIC

# One more entry, past the 39 above, for a different reason. CA_GRANT_ITEM IS
# granted in lib/ (so assertion 4 in check_ability_descs.sh requires it to
# land in this file or in ability_descs.live), but it has no ClassAbilities
# name row and never will: it is not an ability a character holds, it is a
# delivery mechanism, and Player::GainAbility (src/Create.cpp:3584-3589)
# zeroes it the instant it fires ("Abilities[ab] = 0;"). It is excluded from
# ability_descs.live by name (docs/specs/2026-09-20-ability-descriptions-
# spec.md, "Scope"), and recorded here instead so the ratchet has somewhere
# to put it.
CA_GRANT_ITEM
